name: Literal finding locations remain distinct across source revisions and triage
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN SEMGREP_AGENT_TOKEN
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 SEMGREP_ENABLE_VERSION_CHECK=0
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/literal_review.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET/owned
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
paste-file: @ART/open-spaced.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 " app /lib.py":2 | literal-source
expect: print("OWNER_POLICY_REVIEW")
expect-not: live source missing or changed
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 20 " app /lib.py":2 | queue-160x48
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 20 " app /lib.py":2 | queue-96x89
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 20 " app /lib.py":2 | queue-80x24
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 20 " app /lib.py":2 | queue-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 " app /lib.py":2 | queue-40x12
ask: Can the operator distinguish the quoted spaced directory from app/lib.py at all six sizes, without changing the selected finding or its source evidence?
resize: 120x36
submit: decision fp Owned policy marker is intentional source text
paste-file: @ART/open-spaced.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: rejected_false_positive | baseline-fp
nav-mode:
keys: Escape
type: operator draft keep
require-live-snap: 20 operator draft keep | draft-before-revision
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/literal_review.py @TMP_TARGET @ART later
live-snap: draft-after-revision
expect: operator draft keep
keys: C-u
submit: findings
paste-file: @ART/open-spaced.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 different commit | retained-verdict
expect: Reassess this verdict
expect: " app /lib.py":2
ask: Does a later observation keep the human FP decision and literal path while clearly requiring source reassessment across the two real fixture SHAs?
submit: runs diff literal-base literal-later
require-live-snap: 25 SEEN AGAIN | source-comparison
expect: " app /lib.py":2
expect: Absence does not establish a fix.
keys: Tab
require-live-snap: 20 content: | revision-identities
expect: 7cac9e253984
expect: c557cdbf94b9
expect: dirty
keys: Escape
paste-file: @ART/filter-spaced.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 1 of 1 | exact-file-filter
expect: " app /lib.py":2
paste-file: @ART/open-spaced.txt
keys: Enter
submit: decision needs_review Reopen the owned observation on the later source
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: needs_review | reopened-decision
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/literal_review.py @TMP_TARGET @ART reopened
submit: decision fp Owned policy marker rechecked on the later source
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: rejected_false_positive | reassessed-fp
paste-file: @ART/open-plain.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 app/lib.py:2 | plain-source
expect: Owned later observation
submit: decision deferred Owner will assess the ordinary directory separately
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | deferred-decision
submit: findings filter clear
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 2 findings | report
keys: j j j
require-live-snap: 20 format json (4/6) | json-format
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 EXPORTED | exported
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/literal_review.py @TMP_TARGET @ART final
ask: Do reopening, renewed FP and deferral stay attached to the correct literal paths, with original paths preserved in JSON and no inferred fix from the SHA change?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 SEMGREP_ENABLE_VERSION_CHECK=0 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET/owned
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/open-spaced.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 " app /lib.py":2 | recovered-literal-path
expect: false_positive
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 " app /lib.py":2 | recovered-40x12
resize: 120x36
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 2 findings | recovered-report
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/literal_review.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart retain four observations, four human decision events and two distinct literal finding identities without another scan or model request?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
